DOCUMENT();

#############
# Load Macros
#############

loadMacros(
  "PGstandard.pl",
  "PGML.pl",
  "AnswerFormatHelp.pl",
  "parserNumberWithUnits.pl",
  "ORCCA.pl",
  "PGcourse.pl",
);
COMMENT('Authored in PreTeXt');

#######
# Setup
#######

Context('Numeric');
$v = random(45, 90, 1);
$t = random(1, int(($v + sqrt($v**2 + 64*6))/32), 1);
$h = NumberWithUnits(-16*$t**2 + $v*$t + 6, 'ft');

#############################
# Exercise Group Introduction
#############################

BEGIN_PGML
On Earth, if you throw a baseball straight up at speed [`v`] (in feet per second), the height of the ball [`t`] seconds later is given by [`-16t^2+vt+6\text{.}`]

END_PGML

######
# Body
######

BEGIN_PGML
If thrown straight up with speed [`[$v]`] feet per second, how high up is the baseball after [`[$t]`] seconds?

[_]{$h}{10}

END_PGML

#############
# End Problem
#############

ENDDOCUMENT();
